<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charlesfort</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1562</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charlesfort was a short-lived French Huguenot outpost built in 1562 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-ribault">Jean Ribault</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parris-island">Parris Island</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a>. Ribault left a small garrison there while he returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, but supplies failed to arrive and the men abandoned it in 1563. The Spanish later built their town of Santa Elena on the same site, where archaeologists have identified its remains.</p></div>
